---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StartPageGallery from '../../components/StartPageGallery.astro';
import '../../styles/start-page.css';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Start Page Widgets, Wallpaper and Mahjong | Blanc Browser"
  description="Blanc’s Start Page: a clock, your regular sites and the widgets you turn on, over a time-of-day scene, your own image or a color, with standalone Mahjong in the footer."
  path="/features/start-page"
  page="feature-start-page"
  current="features"
  ogImage="/feature-start-page.png"
  ogImageAlt="Blanc’s Start Page with a large clock, local frequent sites, and named groups."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline slot="head">
{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://blanc.day/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Features","item":"https://blanc.day/features"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"Start Page","item":"https://blanc.day/features/start-page"}]}
  </script>
<main id="main-content" class="feature-page feature-detail-page start-page-showcase">
  <section class="sp-stage" aria-labelledby="start-page-title">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/features">features</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">start page</span></nav>
    <div class="sp-stage-copy">
      <h1 id="start-page-title">Make your Start Page your own.</h1>
      <p>A clock, your regular sites and the widgets you choose, over a time-of-day scene, your own image or a color. The footer also opens Mahjong in its own tab and leaves your Start Page in place.</p>
    </div>
    <StartPageGallery />
  </section>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid feature-copy-grid--top" aria-labelledby="start-page-section-0">
    <div><h2 id="start-page-section-0">Widgets, where you want them.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Turn on the widgets you want</h3><p>Open Customize on the Start Page and, under Widgets, turn on Favorites or On your other devices. Each one is a card beside the clock.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Move them and size them</h3><p>Drag a card by its grip to either side of the page, or move it with the arrow keys. Drag its bottom edge to make it taller or shorter; double-click the edge to return it to its automatic size.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Choose how many shortcuts</h3><p>Shortcuts in Customize shows from 1 to 12 of your regular sites under the clock.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Tabs sent to you</h3><p>When another of your devices sends you a tab, it waits on a Sent to this device card.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Coming from another layout</h3><p>If you used Ledger, Shelf or Tally, your Start Page keeps what it showed.</p></article>
    </div>
    <figure class="sp-clock-shot released-capture"><img src="/feature-captures/start-widgets-v1.51.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Blanc’s Start Page over Van Gogh’s Wheat Field with Cypresses, the painting running up behind the Island. A frosted Favorites card on the left lists nine favorites, and the clock reads 4:14 above 328 ads blocked this week and six shortcuts." /></figure>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="start-page-wallpaper-title">
    <div><h2 id="start-page-wallpaper-title">Your own image, or a color.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Use your own image</h3><p>Open Customize on the Start Page and choose Your image under Wallpaper to show a JPEG or PNG of your own, up to 25 MB. Settings → General → Start Page image offers the same choice.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Keep the page readable</h3><p>Wash covers your image so the page stays easy to read: Auto follows your theme, Light and Dark pick one whatever your theme, and Spotlight washes only behind the content. Fade sets how strongly the wash covers the image, down to none.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Your image stays on this device</h3><p>Blanc keeps a resized copy with location, camera and time details removed. It isn’t synced, and private tabs never show it.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Or paint it a color</h3><p>Choose Color under Wallpaper for one of the eight colors Spaces use, as a Soft, Solid or Gradient fill.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Match each space</h3><p>Turn on Match each space’s color, and a window that belongs to a space shows that space’s color on its Start Page.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Up behind the Island</h3><p>Sunrise, a color or your own image continues up behind the Island.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="layout-gallery layout-gallery--pairs" aria-label="Start Page wallpapers: your own image and a color">
    <figure><a href="/feature-captures/start-page-image-v1.41.0.png" aria-label="View full capture of the Start Page with your own image"><img src="/feature-captures/start-page-image-v1.41.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Blanc’s Start Page over Van Gogh’s Wheat Field with Cypresses, with the Spotlight wash behind the clock and favorites." /></a><figcaption>Your image with the Spotlight wash. Van Gogh, Wheat Field with Cypresses, The Met (public domain).</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><a href="/feature-captures/start-page-image-customize-v1.41.0.png" aria-label="View full capture of Customize with Your image selected"><img src="/feature-captures/start-page-image-customize-v1.41.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Customize popover on the Start Page with Your image selected under Wallpaper, a preview of the painting, and the Wash and Fade controls." /></a><figcaption>Customize → Wallpaper → Your image</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><a href="/feature-captures/start-page-color-v1.41.0.png" aria-label="View full capture of the Start Page in a color"><img src="/feature-captures/start-page-color-v1.41.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Blanc’s Start Page painted in the Sky color with the Gradient fill." /></a><figcaption>Color: Sky with the Gradient fill</figcaption></figure>
    <figure><a href="/feature-captures/start-page-color-customize-v1.41.0.png" aria-label="View full capture of Customize with Color selected"><img src="/feature-captures/start-page-color-customize-v1.41.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Customize popover with Color selected under Wallpaper, the eight color swatches, the Fill choice and the Match each space’s color switch." /></a><figcaption>Customize → Wallpaper → Color</figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="start-page-clock-title">
    <div><h2 id="start-page-clock-title">Make the clock your own.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Font, weight and height</h3><p>Right-click the clock, or open Customize and choose Clock. Pick Instrument Sans, Instrument Sans Condensed, Inter or Roboto Flex, then set its weight and, with Instrument Sans or Roboto Flex, how tall it stands.</p></article>
      <article><h3>A color, or glass</h3><p>Keep Automatic, which follows your theme, or pick one of the eight Spaces colors and a tone. Glass bends whatever is behind the numerals; Solid draws them flat.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Readable on any wallpaper</h3><p>Every clock has a soft shadow. When the system asks for reduced transparency, Glass draws as Solid.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Follows you</h3><p>Your clock style syncs with Profile Sync.</p></article>
    </div>
    <figure class="sp-clock-shot released-capture"><a href="/feature-captures/clock-sheet-v1.41.0.png" aria-label="View full capture of the Font & color sheet"><img src="/feature-captures/clock-sheet-v1.41.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Font & color sheet open below a tall glass clock on the Start Page: four font samples, the Weight and Height sliders, nine color choices and Glass or Solid." /></a></figure>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="start-page-section-1">
    <div><h2 id="start-page-section-1">Your regular sites, a click away.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Built from your own visits</h3><p>Your shortcuts are ranked from ordinary browsing history on this device. Their site icons come from locally cached artwork; drawing the row makes no new request to those sites or a favicon service.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Hide a tile without erasing a visit</h3><p>Hide a site from your shortcuts when you do not want it there. That choice stays local and does not delete its history. Private tabs neither contribute to nor receive the history-derived row.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="feature-copy-grid" aria-labelledby="start-page-section-2">
    <div><h2 id="start-page-section-2">Eight boards. A different Daily deal.</h2></div>
    <div class="feature-copy-list">
      <article><h3>Standalone Mahjong</h3><p>Open a standalone Mahjong solitaire table from any start-page footer. Your start page stays open while the game runs in its own managed tab.</p></article>
      <article><h3>A board with a solution</h3><p>Turtle, Arch, Peaks, Pyramid, Fortress, Butterfly, Bridge, and Cross are solvable by construction when dealt. The Daily deal rotates across all eight; your choices during play can still leave you needing a hint, Undo, or Shuffle.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Play at your own pace</h3><p>Choose Classic or Burst, with scoring, timed combos and automatic clears in Burst. Hints, sound controls, Undo, and Shuffle are built in. Shuffle itself can be undone, including after a Burst rescue.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Three tile sets</h3><p>Tiles come in Porcelain, Carved and Inlay. Clear three boards in a row and your next deal moves to the next set.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Keep a record of your progress</h3><p>The Records sheet keeps boards cleared, best Classic times and Burst scores, and current and longest Daily streaks on this device.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Continue an unfinished board</h3><p>Blanc remembers your last board, mode, and deal choice. A new Mahjong tab can offer to continue an unfinished game from another tab.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="layout-gallery" aria-label="Standalone Mahjong">
    <figure><a href="/feature-captures/mahjong-refresh-v1.49.0.png" aria-label="View full standalone Mahjong capture"><img src="/feature-captures/mahjong-refresh-v1.49.0.webp" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Mahjong in Blanc on the Turtle board in Burst mode, with cream tiles on a pale sunrise background and the Burst rack in a column beside the board." /></a><figcaption>Standalone Mahjong — Turtle / Burst</figcaption></figure>
  </section>
  <aside class="truth-note" aria-labelledby="start-page-note-title">
    <h2 id="start-page-note-title">Your game and frequent sites stay on this device.</h2>
    <p>Mahjong games, records, and streaks are not cloud-synced. Your shortcuts’ ranking, cached artwork, and hidden tiles also stay local, and so do your widgets, where they sit, their sizes and your shortcut count. If you enable usage measurement, Blanc can count the first real Mahjong move per app session, without game state or browsing data; private-tab feature activity is excluded.</p>
    <p>Your Start Page color and clock choices can sync through Personal’s optional Sync, while your own image stays on this device.</p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/privacy" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="start-page" data-cta-position="related-feature">Read the data details <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </aside>
  <section class="feature-close" aria-labelledby="start-page-close-title">
    <h2 id="start-page-close-title">Make room for the way you browse.</h2>
    <a class="cta" href="/download" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="start-page" data-cta-position="feature-close">Download Blanc</a>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
